## Bug found

`src/plugin/weekYear/index.js` only handled the "December date belonging to next year's week 1" direction. It was missing the opposite boundary: a **January date that belongs to the last week (52/53) of the previous week-year**. Because `weekOfYear` (src/plugin/weekOfYear/index.js) honours `yearStart` (ISO-8601 style, `yearStart: 4`), `week()` can return 52/53 while `month() === 0` (January) — e.g. 2021-01-01 → week 53 of 2020, 2016-01-01 → week 53 of 2015. The old code returned the calendar year in those cases, which is why the `yearStart: 4` behaviour test failed. With the default `yearStart: 1` this branch is unreachable (January is always week 1), which is why existing tests passed.

## Fix (minimal, only in src/plugin/weekYear/index.js)

```diff
@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@ export default (o, c) => {
     if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
       return year + 1
     }
+    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
+      return year - 1
+    }
     return year
   }
 }
```

No other source file was touched (the only other modified file in `git status` is `src/plugin/timezone/index.js`, owned by another subagent; `scratch-tz.js` is also not mine). No test files modified.

